{"id":"r7","level":1,"levelName":"Reading","n":7,"of":8,"title":"Vowels: i, o, u — and the one that says nothing","titleHe":"נִקּוּד: i, o, u","goal":"Finish the vowel system, including the shva.","sections":[{"type":"vowels","ids":["ִ","ֹ","ֻ","ְ"],"items":[{"sign":"ִ","on":"בִ","name":"חִירִיק","en":"chirik","sound":"i as in machine"},{"sign":"ֹ","on":"בֹ","name":"חוֹלָם","en":"cholam","sound":"o as in more"},{"sign":"ֻ","on":"בֻ","name":"קֻבּוּץ","en":"kubutz","sound":"u as in flute"},{"sign":"ְ","on":"בְ","name":"שְׁוָא","en":"shva","sound":"a half-vowel, or nothing at all"}]},{"type":"text","body":"Two of these are also written with a vav standing in the line rather than a mark underneath."},{"type":"vavvowels","items":[{"on":"בּוֹ","name":"חוֹלָם מָלֵא","en":"cholam male","sound":"o — a vav with a dot above"},{"on":"בּוּ","name":"שׁוּרוּק","en":"shuruk","sound":"u — a vav with a dot in its middle"}]},{"type":"tip","body":"שְׁוָא is the tricky one. At the start of a syllable it's a very short uh; at the end of one it's silent. In בְּרָכָה it sounds (bracha); in יִכְתֹּב it doesn't (yichtov)."}],"vocab":[{"he":"אִישׁ","en":"man","translit":"ish"},{"he":"עִיר","en":"city","translit":"ir"},{"he":"כֹּל","en":"all","translit":"kol"},{"he":"גָּדוֹל","en":"big","translit":"gadol"},{"he":"שֻׁלְחָן","en":"table","translit":"shulchan"},{"he":"בְּרָכָה","en":"blessing","translit":"bracha"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","e as in they","a as in father","i as in machine"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בִ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["e as in they","o as in more","a as in father","a as in father"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בֹ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","u as in flute","a as in father","e as in they"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בֻ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What sound does this vowel make?","options":["a as in father","a half-vowel, or nothing at all","a as in father","e as in they"],"correct":1,"prompt":"בְ"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["fish","see you, goodbye","man","with me"],"correct":2,"prompt":"אִישׁ","translit":"ish"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["does, makes","month","city","blessing"],"correct":2,"prompt":"עִיר","translit":"ir"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["hello, peace","city","gets dressed","all"],"correct":3,"prompt":"כֹּל","translit":"kol"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “table”?","options":["כֶּסֶף","אֵיזֶה","שֻׁלְחָן","כָּאן"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is chirik?","options":["בֵ","בִ","בָ","בַ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is cholam?","options":["בֵ","בָ","בֹ","בַ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “big”?","options":["גָּדוֹל","אֵין","עַל","שָׁלוֹם"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["בְּרָכָה","כֹּל","שֻׁלְחָן","עִיר"],"correct":0,"say":"בְּרָכָה","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Which mark is kubutz?","options":["בָ","בֻ","בֵ","בַ"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “blessing”?","options":["בֵּן","כֹּה","בְּרָכָה","שֶׁ"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"read","he":"אִישׁ","translit":"ish","en":"man"},{"type":"match","pairs":[["בְּרָכָה","blessing"],["עִיר","city"],["כֹּל","all"],["אִישׁ","man"],["גָּדוֹל","big"]]}]}